  "subtitle-win": [
    "France, Spain, Portugal, and England lead the trader consensus for the 2026 World Cup winner, reflecting their balanced squads, recent major-tournament pedigree, and depth heading into the expanded 48-team group stage. Spain enters as reigning European champions with emerging talents like Lamine Yamal, while France relies on Kylian Mbapp\u00e9 and squad versatility despite some pre-tournament injury management. Portugal and England feature strong attacking options and experience, though minor fitness concerns around key players persist. Argentina\u2019s defending-champion status and Brazil\u2019s traditional threat keep them competitive, but early group results and the demanding schedule across North America have kept probabilities tightly clustered among the top European sides rather than creating clear separation."
  ],
  "subtitle-final": [
    "France and Spain lead trader consensus for 2026 World Cup finalists, reflecting their depth, attacking quality, and recent results. France benefits from Kylian Mbapp\u00e9\u2019s form and a favorable group, while Spain\u2019s midfield control and Lamine Yamal\u2019s creativity sustain support despite an opening draw with Cape Verde. England, Portugal, Argentina, and Brazil sit in the next tier, with England\u2019s consistency and Argentina\u2019s experience providing realistic paths through the expanded 48-team bracket. Early group results, including upsets like Ivory Coast over Ecuador, have produced minor odds shifts but not altered the hierarchy. Key upcoming variables include injury updates, rest management in the group stage, and how European sides handle the North American heat and travel before the knockout rounds begin."
